 KUZUSHI > help · mode:shell · target:none · ctx:not built · model:unconfigured

 -- HELP ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Input: ? opens help; ?text, /ask <question>, and ask <question> enter agent mode.
Glossary: TP=true positive; FP=false positive; DFD=data-flow diagram; taint-iris=source-to-sink hunt; x-ray=architecture
review; randori=threat model; tob/shinsa=plugin adapters.
Examples: demo  ·  next  ·  use semgrep  ·  run .  ·  findings  ·  open F-0001  ·  model 1

NAVIGATION — browse modules and tools
home - open Kuzushi cockpit home
  aliases / examples: /home, /
help - show grouped shell help
  aliases / examples: /help, /h, h, ?
workbench - open the split-pane command center
  aliases / examples: /workbench, /studio, /cc, studio, cc
modules - browse native Rust modules
  aliases / examples: /modules, /m, m, show modules
recommend - open latest module recommendations
  aliases / examples: /recommend, rec, /rec
tools [query] - list or filter routed Rust tools
  aliases / examples: /tools, show tools, tools semgrep
doctor - show shell preflight health
  aliases / examples: /doctor, health, /health
use <module> - focus a module
  aliases / examples: use semgrep, /use <module>
back - return to the previous view
  aliases / examples: /back, /b, b
quickstart - first-run guided setup
  aliases / examples: /quickstart
onboarding - open the planning-stage multi-select picker
  aliases / examples: /onboarding, /setup, /planning, /plan-stage
next - continue the engagement (alias: continue) — open the current phase's picker
  aliases / examples: /next
phase <map|hunt|confirm|fix> - open a specific engagement phase picker
  aliases / examples: phase map, phase hunt, phase confirm, phase fix
logs - scrollable full-screen transcript
  aliases / examples: /logs, log, transcript, /transcript

RUN / SCAN — dispatch tools and scans
demo - run a 90-second offline fixture scan; no key, model, or external scanner
  aliases / examples: /demo
scan [target] - open the guided workflow for a target; `scan .` opts into cwd
  aliases / examples: scan ., /scan [target]
run <tool> [json] - dispatch a tool; run . is shell-only focused-module shorthand
  aliases / examples: run ., /run <tool> [json], run . [json]
ask <question> - explicit agent question
  aliases / examples: /ask <question>, ?text

OPTIONS / TASKS — options + sast task control
options [tool] - show tool options
  aliases / examples: /options [tool]
show options [tool] - show tool options
  aliases / examples: /show options [tool]
show advanced [tool] - advanced and evasion options
  aliases / examples: /show advanced [tool]
show missing [tool] - required options without values
  aliases / examples: /show missing [tool]
set <key> <value> - set a session option or shell preference
  aliases / examples: /set <key> <value>
setg <key> <value> - set a persistent option or shell preference
  aliases / examples: /setg <key> <value>
unset <key> - clear a session option or shell preference
  aliases / examples: /unset <key>
unsetg <key> - clear a persistent option or shell preference
  aliases / examples: /unsetg <key>
tasks - choose SAST scanner tasks
  aliases / examples: /tasks
strategy - show proposed phase strategies
  aliases / examples: /strategy, strategies, strategy queue
strategy approve <id> - approve a queued strategy proposal
  aliases / examples: /strategy approve <id>
strategy reject <id> - reject a queued strategy proposal
  aliases / examples: /strategy reject <id>
strategy correct <id> <strategy> - record a strategy correction
  aliases / examples: /strategy correct <id> <strategy>, strategy correct <id> <strategy> --workspace
task block <id> - block a SAST task
  aliases / examples: task deny <id>, /task block <id>
task allow <id> - allow a SAST task
  aliases / examples: /task allow <id>, task unblock <id>
task toggle [id] - toggle a SAST task
  aliases / examples: /task toggle [id]
task mode auto|manual|toggle - switch SAST task selection
  aliases / examples: /task mode auto|manual|toggle
task reset - reset SAST task state
  aliases / examples: /task reset

CONTEXT / KB — workspace + attachments
context - show current context snapshot
  aliases / examples: /context
context build - build repository context
  aliases / examples: /context build
context status - show context status
  aliases / examples: /context status
context regen <slice> - rebuild all, repo, or app-model
  aliases / examples: /context regen <slice>
project - show the aggregated project model
  aliases / examples: /project, project model, project-model
kb [module] - show local KB attachments
  aliases / examples: attachments, /kb [module]
attach <path-or-url> - record local file or URL metadata; omit the path to browse target files
  aliases / examples: /attach <path-or-url>, attach, /attach
files - open a fuzzy target-file picker for KB attachment
  aliases / examples: /files, file-picker, /file-picker
detach <id> - remove a KB attachment
  aliases / examples: /detach <id>
reparse <id> - refresh local attachment metadata
  aliases / examples: /reparse <id>
workspace - show target and state status
  aliases / examples: /workspace, workspace status
workspace export findings <path> [format] - export findings; extensionless defaults to markdown-bundle, or pass
json/jsonl/sarif/csv
  aliases / examples: /workspace export findings <path> [format], findings export <path> [format]
workspace scope init - write an editable .kuzushi/scope.toml scaffold
  aliases / examples: /workspace scope init

FINDINGS / EVIDENCE — browse findings, evidence, and report output
findings - open persisted findings
  aliases / examples: /f, f, /findings
findings filter <expr> - open filtered findings in the Workbench
  aliases / examples: findings filter state:new rank:high, /findings filter <expr>
component <scope|path|all> - focus Workbench findings on a detected component
  aliases / examples: component web/app, component entrypoint-cmd-proxy, component all
open <id> - open a finding alias or fingerprint
  aliases / examples: open F-0001, /open <id>
show aliases [prefix] - list finding aliases
  aliases / examples: /show aliases [prefix]
show runs - recent run artifacts
  aliases / examples: /show runs, runs, /runs
runs diff <left> <right> - compare findings snapshots from two runs
  aliases / examples: runs diff <runA> <runB>, runs compare <runA> <runB>
replay <run|latest> - render a run summary
  aliases / examples: /replay <run|latest>, replay latest
trace <run> - stream run events
  aliases / examples: /trace <run>
activity - live module-progress dashboard
  aliases / examples: /activity, progress, /progress, /a
handoff - latest bounded failure handoff
  aliases / examples: /handoff, failure, /failure
since <ref> - scope findings to a git ref
  aliases / examples: /since <ref>
threats [1-4] - threat model views
  aliases / examples: /threats [1-4], threats summary, threats dfd, threats stride, threats stories, threats scope
threats edit - open the editable threat model view
  aliases / examples: /threats edit
threats regen - Haiku-driven threat-model patch; review then /threats apply
  aliases / examples: /threats regen
threats ask <question> - ask the agent about the current threat model
  aliases / examples: /threats ask <question>
threats apply - apply the pending threat-model patch
  aliases / examples: /threats apply
threats reject - discard the pending threat-model patch
  aliases / examples: /threats reject

AUTH / CONFIG / MODEL — auth, model, runtime config
auth - show env/OAuth status without secrets
  aliases / examples: /auth, auth status
auth login <provider> [method] - start supported OAuth login flow
  aliases / examples: /auth login openai, /auth login anthropic, /auth login github-copilot
provider - show LangGraph provider choices
  aliases / examples: /provider
backend - show Rust runtime backend
  aliases / examples: /backend
model [choice] - select explicit provider:model
  aliases / examples: model 1, /model [choice]
cost - show known session cost estimate
  aliases / examples: /cost
config - show runtime config status
  aliases / examples: /config
permissions - show approval and sandbox policy
  aliases / examples: /permissions, show permissions
target [path] - switch scan target without restart
  aliases / examples: /target [path]
target rev <ref> - switch target git revision when worktree is clean
  aliases / examples: /target rev <sha>, target revision <ref>

SESSION — history, cost, lifecycle
history - show command history
  aliases / examples: /history
clear - clear conversation log
  aliases / examples: /clear
load <specifier> - static registry status or load error
  aliases / examples: /load <specifier>
pause - document live-control absence
  aliases / examples: /pause
cancel - cancel the active scan/tool/agent without leaving the shell
  aliases / examples: /cancel, c, /c, stop, /stop
resume [runId] - document checkpoint-resume absence
  aliases / examples: /resume [runId]
story - show session story replacements
  aliases / examples: /story
prompts - prompt override view
  aliases / examples: /prompts, show prompts
prompt <verb> - prompt editor action
  aliases / examples: /prompt <verb>
tune - module controls
  aliases / examples: /tune, /t, t
actor <n> - actor transcript detail
  aliases / examples: /actor <n>
plan <english> - Haiku natural-language planner; review then /yes or /no
